# One of the four roles from SP-A02-1. Which one a node takes is the boot value `role`, read from
# a credential by workpod-role-generator; the image is the same artifact either way (AB-A02-1).
#
# `control` is the control layer: the plane, the scheduler, both gates and the state database, which
# E-02 rules is the only one. It is also the only role whose disk keeps something across a
# reinstall (`/data/db`, SP-A05-1) and the only one that needs no enrollment token (SP-A04-1).
#
# Wants=, not Requires=: the role names what belongs to it, and the sequence's own Requires-chain
# (disk → selftest → serve) is what enforces A-04.

[Unit]
Description=Workpod node role: control
Documentation=https://github.com/Cheety/warft/blob/main/01-specification.md
Wants=workpod-control.slice
Wants=workpod-disk.service workpod-db.service workpod-selftest.service
Wants=workpod-control.service
